# Story 85: Pipeline Mode (45s)
# Hook: A tab can become a pipeline. One key flips it on and your events start flowing.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-085-pipeline-mode.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
A tab can become a pipeline. One key flips it on and your events start flowing.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Start rysh. Any tab can be promoted into a pipeline tab, where events orchestrate work across panes.

[00:08.0 --> 00:16.0]
Press Ctrl+P to enter pane mode, then p to toggle pipeline mode for this tab.

[00:16.0 --> 00:24.0]
You can also do it from rysh mode. Double-Escape over, then ##tab pipeline enable turns it on explicitly.

[00:24.0 --> 00:32.0]
##tab list confirms the tab is now pipeline-enabled, ready to load and run pipelines.

[00:32.0 --> 00:40.0]
When you're done, ##tab pipeline disable turns it back off -- or just double-Escape, which toggles pipeline mode off.

[00:40.0 --> 00:45.0]
Pipeline mode is the on-switch for event-driven orchestration across your panes.

